# CRM frontend API target. Vite reads this at dev-server start — RESTART
# `npm run dev` after changing it (env vars are not hot-reloaded).
#
# ── OPTION A: LOCAL backend (https://ezyenquiry-backend.onrender.com) ─────────────────────────
# Use this to exercise local backend changes — e.g. the /api/retailer/admin/*
# endpoints that feed the Retailer Management tabs. Start the API first:
#     cd EzyEnquiry-backend && npm run dev
# Caveat: files uploaded to production are NOT on your disk, so document
# previews (KYC, POD images) will 404 locally.
# VITE_API_URL=https://ezyenquiry-backend.onrender.com/api
#
# ── OPTION B: PRODUCTION (Render) — ACTIVE ─────────────────────────────────
# KYC documents/files live here, so document previews work.
# IMPORTANT: this deployment only has the endpoints that were DEPLOYED.
# Any route added to the backend source but not yet pushed will 404 here, and
# the Retailer Management page will show a "sections failed to load" banner.
VITE_API_URL=https://ezyenquiry-backend.onrender.com/api
